.TH AUDITXS 8 "2026" "AuditXS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
auditxs \- transparent, reversible Linux security auditing and hardening
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B auditxs
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B AuditXS
audits a Linux system against fundamental, professional security baselines
(CIS Benchmark / DISA STIG aligned, mapped to NIST CSF 2.0) and \(em only with
explicit consent \(em hardens it with fully reversible changes.
.PP
It is built on three principles:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B Transparent:
.B "auditxs audit"
is strictly read-only. Every check documents what it inspects, why it
matters, exactly what its fix changes and how that change is reverted.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Reversible:
before anything is modified it is copied into a timestamped snapshot;
.B "auditxs rollback"
restores it.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Consented:
fixes are applied one at a time after review, with
.B \-\-dry\-run
to preview and
.B \-\-yes
for automation.
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B audit
Run all applicable checks (read-only). Saves HTML and JSON reports and prints
a severity-weighted hardening score and a CVE warning banner.
.TP
.B harden
Review failed checks and apply fixes one by one, with consent.
.TP
.B rollback \fR<id>|latest\fP
Revert a hardening snapshot.
.TP
.B snapshots
List change snapshots.
.TP
.B list \fR[--markdown]\fP
Show the check catalogue (or full documentation).
.TP
.B explain \fR<ID>...\fP
Show full documentation for checks, including CIS id, level and NIST mapping.
.TP
.B report \fR--format html|json|tsv\fP
Print a report of a fresh audit to stdout.
.TP
.B diff \fR<baseline.json> [current.json]\fP
Compare two saved reports; exits non-zero on regressions.
.TP
.B baseline \fRset|show|clear\fP
Manage the approved baseline used for drift detection.
.TP
.B schedule \fRenable|disable|status|run\fP
Daily audit with baseline drift alerting (systemd timer).
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnose the installation, tooling and snapshot integrity.
.TP
.B cve
Warn about installed packages with a known vulnerability / CVE.
.TP
.B tools \fRstatus|install|scan|vpn\fP
Install and run security tools (Lynis, rkhunter, CrowdSec, Suricata, \[char46]\[char46]\[char46]);
review VPN configuration.
.TP
.B web \fR[--port N] [--no-open]\fP
Launch the local Material Design web UI. Binds 127.0.0.1 only and requires an
ephemeral token; reach a remote server through an SSH tunnel.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-profile server|workstation
Override the configured profile.
.TP
.B \-\-category \fIname\fP
Only checks in one category (e.g. SSH, Firewall).
.TP
.B \-\-domain \fIname\fP
Only one assessment domain (Server, OS, Network, Application, Database).
.TP
.B \-\-level 1|2
Only CIS Level \(<= N checks (2 includes 1).
.TP
.B \-\-framework cis
Only checks carrying a CIS Benchmark reference.
.TP
.B \-\-check \fIID\fP
Only this check (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-format text|tsv|json|html
Output format.
.TP
.B \-\-baseline \fIreport.json\fP
Compare audit results against a saved report.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
harden: show every intended change without applying it.
.TP
.B \-\-yes\fR, \fP\-y
Assume "yes" to confirmations (automation).
.TP
.B \-\-quiet\fR, \fP\-q
Suppress progress output.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Verbose diagnostics (timings, return codes).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/auditxs/auditxs.conf
Profile configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/auditxs/baseline.json
Approved baseline (optional).
.TP
.I /var/lib/auditxs/snapshots/
Rollback snapshots.
.TP
.I /var/lib/auditxs/reports/
HTML/JSON audit reports.
.TP
.I /var/lib/auditxs/changes.log
Append-only ledger of every change AuditXS ever made.
.TP
.I /var/log/auditxs/
Daily logs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B audit
and
.B harden
return 0 on completion (findings do not affect the exit code).
.B diff
and
.B "schedule run"
return non-zero when a regression/drift is detected.
.B cve
returns non-zero when vulnerable packages are found.
.B doctor
returns non-zero when problems are found.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B sudo auditxs audit
Full read-only audit with report and score.
.TP
.B sudo auditxs harden --dry-run
Preview every change without applying it.
.TP
.B sudo auditxs audit --level 1 --framework cis
Audit only CIS Level-1 controls.
.TP
.B sudo auditxs rollback latest
Undo the most recent hardening run.
